3266
03:43:29,720 --> 03:43:30,320
Oh, wait a minute.

3267
03:43:30,860 --> 03:43:32,800
He can level up to something more than an expert?

3268
03:43:34,660 --> 03:43:34,980
What?

3269
03:43:36,320 --> 03:43:37,380
What is the next stage?

3270
03:43:39,840 --> 03:43:40,840
I don't have that many feathers.

3271
03:43:41,000 --> 03:43:41,300
Oh, no.

3272
03:43:44,400 --> 03:43:45,780
I guess I can give him some money.

3273
03:43:46,440 --> 03:43:47,120
Money is fine.

3274
03:43:49,840 --> 03:43:50,880
Where did I leave my money?

3275
03:43:53,320 --> 03:43:53,640
Ah.

3276
03:43:55,120 --> 03:43:55,960
Just a bit of money.

3277
03:44:01,350 --> 03:44:02,130
Let's see.

3278
03:44:04,350 --> 03:44:08,950
Make me... That's not enough.

3279
03:44:09,110 --> 03:44:09,910
That's enough.

3280
03:44:11,190 --> 03:44:11,830
Thirteen.

3281
03:44:12,030 --> 03:44:12,970
Is that worth it, though?

3282
03:44:15,870 --> 03:44:17,530
Probably make arrows instead.

3283
03:44:25,300 --> 03:44:25,860
There.

3284
03:44:28,200 --> 03:44:28,760
Aw!

3285
03:44:29,120 --> 03:44:30,780
Rosie wants to sleep in the bed.

3286
03:44:31,840 --> 03:44:32,400
Master!

3287
03:44:35,020 --> 03:44:36,380
Crossbow with piercing two.

3288
03:44:37,740 --> 03:44:40,280
And I can make tripwire hooks for emeralds.

3289
03:44:41,600 --> 03:44:42,000
Damn.

3290
03:44:43,700 --> 03:44:44,260
Alright.

3291
03:44:45,020 --> 03:44:49,220
I wonder if I can... somehow change these.

3292
03:44:49,380 --> 03:44:50,720
Like, if I don't like this very much.

3293
03:44:55,000 --> 03:44:56,220
You can stay there, Rosie.

3294
03:44:57,540 --> 03:44:58,880
You like the Fletcher, huh?

3295
03:44:59,920 --> 03:45:00,600
That's fine.

3296
03:45:01,900 --> 03:45:04,120
Okay, well, we have a way to get money now.

3297
03:45:04,620 --> 03:45:06,340
What does a tripwire thingy need?

3298
03:45:09,280 --> 03:45:11,420
Sticks... Oh, that's super cheap!

3299
03:45:13,700 --> 03:45:14,540
Oh my god!

3300
03:45:16,020 --> 03:45:16,740
That's money!

3301
03:45:19,900 --> 03:45:20,740
Lots of money!

3302
03:45:21,340 --> 03:45:22,880
What are you doing up there, Rosie?

3303
03:45:27,670 --> 03:45:28,570
Yeah, I know.

3304
03:45:29,990 --> 03:45:31,270
Oh, we also got some money here.

3305
03:45:33,270 --> 03:45:34,030
Very nice.

3306
03:45:35,710 --> 03:45:37,110
We need this, then we need wood.

3307
03:45:39,050 --> 03:45:40,110
We have a bunch of wood.

3308
03:45:40,750 --> 03:45:43,830
And the last thing was... what was it?

3309
03:45:44,190 --> 03:45:44,590
Sticks?

3310
03:45:44,830 --> 03:45:45,650
Oh, we have a lot of that, too.

3311
03:45:47,010 --> 03:45:47,630
So many!

3312
03:45:52,020 --> 03:45:52,680
Ayo, my dude.

3313
03:45:54,820 --> 03:45:55,760
Make me money.

3314
03:46:00,740 --> 03:46:01,100
Nine.

3315
03:46:03,720 --> 03:46:05,220
Oh, now he doesn't want to do that anymore.

3316
03:46:05,920 --> 03:46:06,280
Okay.

3317
03:46:07,320 --> 03:46:09,100
Let's see how long it takes for these to refresh.

3318
03:46:19,260 --> 03:46:19,740
Success!

3319
03:46:20,220 --> 03:46:23,440
We have a villager that has achieved max rank.

3320
03:46:25,740 --> 03:46:27,740
That's a W in my book.

3321
03:46:30,760 --> 03:46:31,840
Put the wood in here.

3322
03:46:34,520 --> 03:46:35,000
Wait.

3323
03:46:35,980 --> 03:46:37,680
That's got to be the anvil I made just before.

3324
03:46:41,040 --> 03:46:41,760
Clock.

3325
03:46:42,580 --> 03:46:43,780
Eyes of Ender.

3326
03:46:43,980 --> 03:46:49,960
Dude, we can make enough end crystals now.

3327
03:46:50,560 --> 03:46:51,740
Oh, man.

3328
03:46:53,520 --> 03:46:54,760
Let's make a bunch.

3329
03:46:56,620 --> 03:46:58,180
Glass and ghast here.

3330
03:46:58,860 --> 03:46:59,900
We can make four more.

3331
03:47:01,340 --> 03:47:02,060
Glass?

3332
03:47:05,700 --> 03:47:07,420
Okay, that's fine, I guess.

3333
03:47:09,640 --> 03:47:10,860
We have five now.

3334
03:47:11,140 --> 03:47:12,880
I forgot how many towers there were.

3335
03:47:13,800 --> 03:47:15,120
I think it's more than five.

3336
03:47:15,300 --> 03:47:17,680
It's like eight, maybe even ten.

3337
03:47:18,060 --> 03:47:18,740
No, not ten.

3338
03:47:19,040 --> 03:47:19,880
Maybe eight or nine.

3339
03:47:20,340 --> 03:47:21,300
Just like a good amount.

3340
03:47:23,940 --> 03:47:25,140
But we're getting there.

3341
03:47:26,140 --> 03:47:27,720
We're getting there, slowly but surely.

3342
03:47:30,240 --> 03:47:31,120
Cool in there.

3343
03:47:32,160 --> 03:47:34,560
Gold, gold, gold, so much crap.

3344
03:47:34,720 --> 03:47:35,240
Oh, this one.

3345
03:47:35,420 --> 03:47:36,000
I hate that.

3346
03:47:36,660 --> 03:47:37,320
Gotta fix it.

3347
03:47:44,240 --> 03:47:44,680
Yep.

3348
03:47:47,240 --> 03:47:47,680
Nice.

3349
03:47:51,460 --> 03:47:52,800
I gotta make a cleric.

3350
03:47:56,220 --> 03:47:58,320
Extra anvil, let's put that in the construction.

3351
03:48:00,720 --> 03:48:05,980
Tripwire hooks... I guess redstone makes the most sense.

3352
03:48:06,680 --> 03:48:10,880
Now, why couldn't I make more... What was the bottleneck?

3353
03:48:13,820 --> 03:48:14,460
Glass.

3354
03:48:14,780 --> 03:48:15,320
Okay.

3355
03:48:16,820 --> 03:48:18,160
Let's cook some sand.

3356
03:48:22,740 --> 03:48:23,480
Mm-hmm.

3357
03:48:23,940 --> 03:48:24,940
Clock in here.

3358
03:48:25,760 --> 03:48:26,440
I guess.

3359
03:48:27,440 --> 03:48:29,000
I don't know, that's not very useful.

3360
03:48:29,180 --> 03:48:30,640
I don't... The clock is weird.

3361
03:48:35,980 --> 03:48:37,360
Gas tier, sticks.

3362
03:48:37,680 --> 03:48:46,800
Oh, sticks is also something we need, right, for the... And... No, it was just gas tier, I have ender, and... Seven.

3363
03:48:48,200 --> 03:48:48,760
Of those.

3364
03:48:49,560 --> 03:48:51,400
And I can get quite a lot out here.

3365
03:48:51,560 --> 03:48:52,400
Okay, it's just gonna take a while.

3366
03:48:53,680 --> 03:48:54,160
That's fine.

3367
03:48:56,870 --> 03:48:57,830
Bone block.

3368
03:48:59,670 --> 03:49:06,650
I would say... Yeah, miscellaneous.

3369
03:49:06,930 --> 03:49:07,970
That's where I already have it.

3370
03:49:11,110 --> 03:49:17,930
We have a furnace, a door, more signs, and a bucket.

3371
03:49:19,290 --> 03:49:22,610
This is the perfect sort of utility pouch for exploration.

3372
03:49:32,160 --> 03:49:32,840
Book in.

3373
03:49:34,000 --> 03:49:35,760
Level 18 is not too bad, actually.

3374
03:49:36,120 --> 03:49:36,840
So look, look, look.

3375
03:49:37,460 --> 03:49:38,180
Flowers open.

3376
03:49:38,360 --> 03:49:38,840
It's night.

3377
03:49:39,480 --> 03:49:39,760
Okay?

3378
03:49:39,980 --> 03:49:40,960
Watch when it becomes day.

3379
03:49:41,100 --> 03:49:41,820
We're gonna check it again.

3380
03:49:42,360 --> 03:49:43,020
It's gonna be closed.

3381
03:49:49,380 --> 03:49:50,680
So many of these bundles.

3382
03:49:52,320 --> 03:49:53,420
Some of them can go in here.

3383
03:50:01,820 --> 03:50:03,240
All the food as well.

3384
03:50:03,860 --> 03:50:13,080
Ah, these all keep... Many emeralds.

3385
03:50:18,660 --> 03:50:20,140
And wheat that is farming.

3386
03:50:21,700 --> 03:50:23,740
Ooh, it's taking a while to sort this inventory, huh?

3387
03:50:25,840 --> 03:50:27,240
So much random crap.

3388
03:50:30,160 --> 03:50:31,380
I do need ten in here.

3389
03:50:31,700 --> 03:50:32,740
Or maybe not that one.

3390
03:50:32,800 --> 03:50:33,500
Put it in mining.

3391
03:50:35,720 --> 03:50:37,080
And the rest goes in here.

3392
03:50:40,640 --> 03:50:41,320
Spruce log.

3393
03:50:44,820 --> 03:50:45,720
Is this done yet?

3394
03:50:45,980 --> 03:50:46,660
Not quite.

3395
03:50:46,860 --> 03:50:47,480
We have 18.

3396
03:50:49,000 --> 03:50:49,800
Actually, that's enough.

3397
03:50:52,940 --> 03:50:56,320
No, I need to end this one.

3398
03:50:57,480 --> 03:50:57,900
Nice.

3399
03:50:59,460 --> 03:51:01,460
Now we have... how many is it?

3400
03:51:01,600 --> 03:51:01,920
Seven?

3401
03:51:02,640 --> 03:51:05,860
Okay, we're approaching, I think, the right amount that we can test with.

3402
03:51:07,900 --> 03:51:08,840
Good, good, good.

3403
03:51:12,660 --> 03:51:13,520
What do we have in here?

3404
03:51:14,280 --> 03:51:19,060
Phantom membrane, sticks, sugarcane, wind charge, bones, and coal.

3405
03:51:19,920 --> 03:51:23,180
I think having coal in here is a good idea for emergency situations.

3406
03:51:27,200 --> 03:51:27,560
Yeah.

3407
03:51:30,620 --> 03:51:32,200
Ah, I like having this in here, I guess.

3408
03:51:38,120 --> 03:51:39,160
Okay, sticks.

3409
03:51:40,680 --> 03:51:41,940
Charge is a drop.

3410
03:51:42,440 --> 03:51:43,160
So is bone.

3411
03:51:44,140 --> 03:51:45,320
Burn this goes over here.

3412
03:51:46,680 --> 03:51:47,280
Soon!

3413
03:51:47,500 --> 03:51:49,240
I actually fixed my inventory, it's insane.

3414
03:51:51,500 --> 03:51:52,520
Ten ominous banners.

3415
03:51:53,360 --> 03:51:54,500
I'm collecting them.

3416
03:51:55,780 --> 03:51:59,560
Let's go check how many sugar can... I saw that close!

3417
03:52:00,540 --> 03:52:02,200
Right in front of my eyes.

3418
03:52:03,400 --> 03:52:05,920
Think you can close without me seeing it, huh?

3419
03:52:09,160 --> 03:52:09,660
Oh.

3420
03:52:11,960 --> 03:52:13,200
Hey, wait a minute.

3421
03:52:14,040 --> 03:52:15,220
You know what I think?

3422
03:52:16,660 --> 03:52:17,920
I just had an idea.

3423
03:52:18,700 --> 03:52:21,860
That's pretty much a daylight detector.

3424
03:52:22,540 --> 03:52:25,500
If that works with Redstone, we can put an observer there.

3425
03:52:26,060 --> 03:52:28,060
The actual model changes, right?

3426
03:52:30,180 --> 03:52:31,040
Let's see here.

3427
03:52:32,760 --> 03:52:35,640
Ah, shit, I don't have it here, but I guarantee it's gonna work.

3428
03:52:36,600 --> 03:52:41,260
And the difference between that and a daylight detector is gonna be it's probably gonna just send one pulse, right?

3429
03:52:41,920 --> 03:52:42,900
It's a one-pulser.

3430
03:52:44,640 --> 03:52:45,740
Oh yeah, right here.

3431
03:52:51,640 --> 03:52:52,500
Nice, not bad.

3432
03:52:52,660 --> 03:52:54,120
I guess I was away from home for a bit.

3433
03:53:04,830 --> 03:53:05,430
Okay.

3434
03:53:05,430 --> 03:53:06,750
I love that horn.

3435
03:53:10,890 --> 03:53:12,050
Look at all this crap.

3436
03:53:12,950 --> 03:53:14,790
Two seek horns and one sing.

3437
03:53:17,370 --> 03:53:18,730
You know what, actually.

3438
03:53:20,470 --> 03:53:21,070
Yes!

3439
03:53:21,610 --> 03:53:22,270
That's beautiful!

3440
03:53:22,550 --> 03:53:24,170
We should have a collection of horns!

3441
03:53:32,250 --> 03:53:33,530
The horn of plenty.

3442
03:53:35,310 --> 03:53:36,070
I like it.

3443
03:53:41,130 --> 03:53:42,610
Oh, they both share a cooldown.

3444
03:53:42,750 --> 03:53:43,210
That's too bad.

3445
03:53:43,330 --> 03:53:44,470
I can't combine the sounds.

3446
03:53:46,270 --> 03:53:47,030
Too bad.

3447
03:53:48,330 --> 03:53:49,810
I was gonna make a little melody.

3448
03:53:51,190 --> 03:53:52,290
You'll need two buckets.

3449
03:53:54,370 --> 03:53:56,350
One bucket is more than enough for one man.

3450
03:54:01,330 --> 03:54:02,870
Four bundles is the perfect amount.

3451
03:54:03,010 --> 03:54:03,510
Changed my mind.

3452
03:54:04,550 --> 03:54:05,530
The rest go in here.

3453
03:54:10,510 --> 03:54:11,350
Shield here.

3454
03:54:11,450 --> 03:54:12,930
They can go up in armor, I guess.

3455
03:54:16,170 --> 03:54:17,210
Same with that one.

3456
03:54:19,210 --> 03:54:20,090
Glasses up here.

3457
03:54:28,070 --> 03:54:29,250
I have a lot of rails.

3458
03:54:31,330 --> 03:54:32,670
I should, in fact, go in the other one.

3459
03:54:35,590 --> 03:54:37,170
Rails, rails, rails...

3460
03:54:43,960 --> 03:54:45,160
I'm gonna need all these.

3461
03:54:46,360 --> 03:54:51,040
I will make a path or a railway to that valley we saw.

3462
03:54:51,260 --> 03:54:57,740
And I'm gonna have a huge mega grassland with farms everywhere.

3463
03:54:58,780 --> 03:55:02,100
I'm gonna have wheat, potatoes, carrots, everything.

3464
03:55:02,940 --> 03:55:04,340
That will be the place.

3465
03:55:06,040 --> 03:55:07,240
Ah, but wait a minute.

3466
03:55:08,860 --> 03:55:10,260
We have a problem here.

3467
03:55:10,900 --> 03:55:14,480
Because that is not gonna simulate while I'm over here.

3468
03:55:14,660 --> 03:55:15,440
It's too far.

3469
03:55:16,620 --> 03:55:17,100
Fuck.

3470
03:55:17,660 --> 03:55:19,360
It needs to be somewhat close.

3471
03:55:21,320 --> 03:55:22,760
God damn it.

3472
03:55:25,100 --> 03:55:25,900
It's fine.

3473
03:55:28,820 --> 03:55:30,900
These are utilities, for sure.

3474
03:55:32,640 --> 03:55:34,140
These two need to be repaired.

3475
03:55:35,360 --> 03:55:37,740
I think we're about back where we were here.

3476
03:55:38,000 --> 03:55:38,440
Grass?

3477
03:55:38,580 --> 03:55:40,080
I don't... I hate that name for that.

3478
03:55:40,720 --> 03:55:42,260
Why the hell did I call it grass?

3479
03:55:43,400 --> 03:55:44,560
That makes no sense.

3480
03:55:46,560 --> 03:55:48,120
A bucket of axolotl.

3481
03:55:48,180 --> 03:55:48,820
Forgot about that.

3482
03:55:49,720 --> 03:55:51,820
Should totally put him in a little pool somewhere.

3483
03:55:55,110 --> 03:55:56,170
You made mending.

3484
03:55:57,730 --> 03:55:58,130
Smite.

3485
03:55:58,410 --> 03:56:05,430
I think the next step... So, what I actually wanted to do today, that I never got to in the beginning, I wanted to expand my village.

3486
03:56:05,930 --> 03:56:07,430
Move the borders, so to speak, here.

3487
03:56:08,910 --> 03:56:10,630
And... make more houses.

3488
03:56:10,910 --> 03:56:12,050
Bring more villagers in.

3489
03:56:12,210 --> 03:56:13,130
Have more jobs.

3490
03:56:14,010 --> 03:56:15,250
In fact, I want a cleric.

3491
03:56:15,310 --> 03:56:16,430
I want to level them all up, you know?

3492
03:56:18,810 --> 03:56:22,570
And maybe there is a way to sort of reset them without killing them.

3493
03:56:22,730 --> 03:56:24,630
I need to think about how that could be done.

3494
03:56:25,830 --> 03:56:27,650
Removing their job here is not gonna work.

3495
03:56:29,210 --> 03:56:30,550
Maybe something else needs to be done.

3496
03:56:30,850 --> 03:56:33,990
Maybe turning them into a zombie somehow will reset them.

3497
03:56:34,250 --> 03:56:35,510
Put them back to a villager.

3498
03:56:35,890 --> 03:56:36,410
You know?

3499
03:56:37,530 --> 03:56:38,390
Something like that.

3500
03:56:41,470 --> 03:56:43,230
Okay, this is a good setup right now.

3501
03:56:44,510 --> 03:56:45,770
I'm ready for next time now.

3502
03:56:46,310 --> 03:56:46,570
Perfect.

3503
03:56:46,930 --> 03:56:47,830
Good time to stop.

3504
03:56:50,290 --> 03:56:50,730
Sensational.

3505
03:57:13,280 --> 03:57:14,320
Fuck, I was muted.

3506
03:57:14,740 --> 03:57:15,340
I'm back.

3507
03:57:15,840 --> 03:57:17,200
What did you think of my retrieval today?

3508
03:57:17,740 --> 03:57:18,360
Tell me.

3509
03:57:19,320 --> 03:57:20,240
Sing my praises.

3510
03:57:22,420 --> 03:57:23,660
I'm so proud of myself.

3511
03:57:26,800 --> 03:57:29,900
I can't tell you how emotionally affected I was by that.

3512
03:57:29,960 --> 03:57:34,060
In the moment when I saw those items down there, I was almost losing my mind.

3513
03:57:37,800 --> 03:57:38,940
I couldn't even talk.

3514
03:57:39,200 --> 03:57:40,520
I just had to collect them.

3515
03:57:40,580 --> 03:57:41,140
I was focusing.

3516
03:57:51,800 --> 03:57:53,520
I was about to leave at that point.

3517
03:57:55,060 --> 03:57:59,480
I mean, I figured I would have to wait, because I had to do something different than last time, right?

3518
03:58:00,080 --> 03:58:01,120
Killing him didn't work.

3519
03:58:01,820 --> 03:58:08,640
And he was shaking, so it made sense to wait, but I waited so long, I thought, okay, maybe I'm not understanding this.

3520
03:58:08,980 --> 03:58:10,360
So I was about to go.

3521
03:58:15,890 --> 03:58:18,510
You were wasting so much time with the mobs, we were freaking out.

3522
03:58:18,610 --> 03:58:20,950
Yeah, but listen, what if I had run in there and died?

3523
03:58:21,170 --> 03:58:22,450
I have to play it safe too, right?

3524
03:58:23,690 --> 03:58:25,350
What, would you just have ignored the mobs?

3525
03:58:26,370 --> 03:58:27,390
They would have followed you.

3526
03:58:31,850 --> 03:58:32,870
Oh, that looks interesting.

3527
03:58:32,950 --> 03:58:33,770
Dirty poop water.

3528
03:58:34,790 --> 03:58:38,030
Well, interesting in a way, it's different than what you usually see.

3529
03:58:38,130 --> 03:58:39,990
I've never seen a waterfall of poop water, have you?

3530
03:58:45,070 --> 03:58:45,730
What's this?

3531
03:58:45,890 --> 03:58:46,770
Pro-Minecrafter?

3532
03:58:46,910 --> 03:58:47,670
Indeed, OneHoop.

3533
03:58:47,770 --> 03:58:48,370
Thanks for subbing.

3534
03:58:50,750 --> 03:58:52,190
And thanks to everyone else, too.

3535
03:58:52,750 --> 03:58:53,810
I see Meepskitten has subbed.

3536
03:58:53,890 --> 03:58:54,890
He's at 13 months now.

3537
03:58:55,230 --> 03:58:55,690
It's insane.

3538
03:58:56,530 --> 03:58:57,010
Thank you.

3539
03:59:00,290 --> 03:59:01,230
Many others, too.

3540
03:59:05,430 --> 03:59:08,450
RT game did a poop volcano in Cities Skylines?

3541
03:59:08,770 --> 03:59:10,070
What does that even mean?

3542
03:59:12,170 --> 03:59:13,650
It sounds great!

3543
03:59:21,090 --> 03:59:23,050
Are you ever going to check out Minecraft servers?

3544
03:59:23,650 --> 03:59:25,030
You mean the community server?

3545
03:59:25,550 --> 03:59:26,450
That we have here?

3546
03:59:26,630 --> 03:59:27,670
Or other servers?

3547
03:59:29,090 --> 03:59:29,850
Other servers?

3548
03:59:29,950 --> 03:59:30,350
I don't know.

3549
03:59:30,990 --> 03:59:32,150
Maybe in the very future.

3550
03:59:33,690 --> 03:59:38,310
I think it would have to be at a point where I'm not finding much enjoyment from the base game as it is right now.

3551
03:59:38,530 --> 03:59:39,690
And needed something different.

3552
03:59:42,490 --> 03:59:44,970
But for now, I'm having a blast with just playing the game.

3553
03:59:47,250 --> 03:59:48,310
You're the goat, Oliver.

3554
03:59:48,450 --> 03:59:48,930
Thanks for streaming.

3555
03:59:49,070 --> 03:59:52,710
Thanks for stopping by and leaving that nice comment.

3556
03:59:56,030 --> 03:59:56,970
Great job, Oliver.

3557
03:59:57,130 --> 03:59:58,390
I have no idea how you found the spot.

3558
03:59:58,630 --> 04:00:00,730
You have to remember, you're a watcher, right?

3559
04:00:00,890 --> 04:00:01,570
I'm a player.

3560
04:00:01,930 --> 04:00:05,090
In the sense that I remember going through these motions.

3561
04:00:05,670 --> 04:00:08,910
So my memory will always be stronger than yours when it comes to this.

3562
04:00:18,410 --> 04:00:21,530
53% of people thought you wouldn't find your items and bring them home.

3563
04:00:22,050 --> 04:00:26,090
Honestly, I'm impressed that almost half believed in me.

3564
04:00:30,570 --> 04:00:34,570
I'm kind of proud of you for that half of you actually believed in me.

3565
04:00:35,230 --> 04:00:36,350
I didn't believe in me.

3566
04:00:38,190 --> 04:00:39,690
It was a long shot, for sure.

3567
04:00:44,730 --> 04:00:53,350
If it wasn't for the fact that the cave that I died in was right next to where I exited, I don't think I would have been able to find it.

3568
04:00:55,570 --> 04:00:56,910
That gave me confidence, right?

3569
04:00:57,370 --> 04:00:59,250
Remembering that it was right when I exited.

3570
04:01:04,570 --> 04:01:06,290
I was burned enough on not believing.

3571
04:01:06,450 --> 04:01:07,110
Team believer now.

3572
04:01:07,910 --> 04:01:08,790
Be careful, though.

3573
04:01:09,070 --> 04:01:14,030
Next time I'm gonna set a goal for something really simple, everyone's gonna be like, he can do it.

3574
04:01:14,430 --> 04:01:15,450
And then I couldn't.

3575
04:01:17,190 --> 04:01:20,970
I will also disappoint in the most surprising ways, you know?

3576
04:01:21,510 --> 04:01:24,430
In the most not-so-great ways, I mean.

3577
04:01:30,940 --> 04:01:33,000
The torch in the cave was such a lifesaver.

3578
04:01:33,120 --> 04:01:33,720
I know!

3579
04:01:35,020 --> 04:01:39,860
When I went down into the cave, or when I saw the cave at first, I actually thought this is not it.

3580
04:01:40,700 --> 04:01:45,960
Because I seem to have a memory of flying around first, and then flying into the cave.

3581
04:01:46,780 --> 04:01:48,840
So I thought maybe I flew into a different cave.

3582
04:01:49,020 --> 04:01:54,340
So if it wasn't for that torch, I may have gone down there, looked around, decided this is not it.

3583
04:01:54,720 --> 04:01:57,200
Went out again, and tried to fly around a bit.

3584
04:02:01,370 --> 04:02:02,930
Do you want to know how many igloos you missed?

3585
04:02:03,070 --> 04:02:03,630
Yeah, actually.

3586
04:02:04,430 --> 04:02:05,270
Did I miss any?

3587
04:02:15,610 --> 04:02:17,150
Did you have an Elytra at that point?

3588
04:02:18,670 --> 04:02:22,110
I must have, because I have a distinct memory of flying around and into the cave.

3589
04:02:24,430 --> 04:02:27,570
Unless I'm actually not... Is that not right?

3590
04:02:28,270 --> 04:02:29,410
Am I imagining that?

3591
04:02:31,650 --> 04:02:33,030
I must have had an Elytra.

3592
04:02:33,210 --> 04:02:33,510
Hold on.

3593
04:02:34,050 --> 04:02:35,330
Don't gaslight me right now.

3594
04:02:36,250 --> 04:02:38,410
Did I have an Elytra when I died back then?

3595
04:02:42,240 --> 04:02:43,120
Yeah, but hold on.

3596
04:02:44,540 --> 04:02:45,980
Well, there wasn't an Elijah there.

3597
04:02:46,160 --> 04:02:46,900
Fuck, you're right!

3598
04:02:50,720 --> 04:02:51,520
Holy shit!

3599
04:02:53,040 --> 04:02:54,500
What am I thinking about then?

3600
04:02:56,160 --> 04:03:00,480
I... I don't know what I'm thinking about!

3601
04:03:01,440 --> 04:03:07,880
I was pretty sure I exited, flew around, and then, because of my hubris, I was trying to fly into the cave.

3602
04:03:09,580 --> 04:03:12,840
Then I flew in there and I got killed by mobs and died to fall damage.

3603
04:03:15,800 --> 04:03:17,660
But I may be mixing memories here.

3604
04:03:17,760 --> 04:03:21,520
Maybe I'm mixing together the memory of flying into the cave next to my house.

3605
04:03:22,240 --> 04:03:23,920
Because I did that too and died there.

3606
04:03:31,340 --> 04:03:34,240
Don't forget your glass railway underwater to the pink tree valley.

3607
04:03:34,360 --> 04:03:35,760
Yeah, don't worry, I haven't forgotten.

3608
04:03:35,920 --> 04:03:37,280
In fact, I wrote it down in my notebook.

3609
04:03:38,660 --> 04:03:39,680
In my goals book.

3610
04:03:39,880 --> 04:03:40,680
It's gonna happen.

3611
04:03:43,260 --> 04:03:45,020
In fact, I'm very excited about that one.

3612
04:03:46,400 --> 04:03:49,960
Maybe it's not gonna be a farm that I have over there, like, with lots of wheat and all that.

3613
04:03:50,600 --> 04:03:51,640
It's just something different.

3614
04:03:52,300 --> 04:03:53,400
Maybe a different village.

3615
04:03:57,810 --> 04:03:59,770
Are there any more items you need to recover?

3616
04:04:00,330 --> 04:04:01,690
I'm not actually sure.

3617
04:04:02,130 --> 04:04:07,830
I was pretty sure that the items I would find today was going to be netherite stuff.

3618
04:04:08,410 --> 04:04:15,470
But that wasn't the case, so I... I must really have mixed together my... memories.

3619
04:04:17,490 --> 04:04:20,190
I don't remember what the hell happened to my netherite.

3620
04:04:21,470 --> 04:04:22,830
I think I may have lost it.

3621
04:04:23,560 --> 04:04:27,200
I seem to remember something in the end, losing some of them there.

3622
04:04:27,940 --> 04:04:30,000
It is all melted together in my mind, yeah.

3623
04:04:44,870 --> 04:04:48,510
I know that some people play this game without ever even touching redstone, right?

3624
04:04:49,270 --> 04:04:52,810
Some people have told me they learned from me doing redstone now, so that's cool.

3625
04:04:55,490 --> 04:05:00,890
Not that the stuff I'm doing is very advanced, but maybe just for understanding's sake, right?

3626
04:05:01,410 --> 04:05:03,010
Some of the blocks...

3627
04:05:06,110 --> 04:05:07,930
The end is never the end is never the end.

3628
04:05:09,370 --> 04:05:10,270
Calm down, Daniel.

3629
04:05:13,440 --> 04:05:15,600
At least you have a bunch of bundles.

3630
04:05:16,280 --> 04:05:18,600
Yeah, but they're not even that worthwhile.

3631
04:05:18,940 --> 04:05:21,500
I mean, um... What do you call it?

3632
04:05:21,700 --> 04:05:22,720
They're not worth that much.

3633
04:05:22,740 --> 04:05:24,760
I can make infinite amounts of those.

3634
04:05:25,040 --> 04:05:26,400
It's not that expensive to make.

3635
04:05:28,180 --> 04:05:29,520
Rosie's my new favorite villager?

3636
04:05:30,800 --> 04:05:31,240
Really?

3637
04:05:31,600 --> 04:05:33,620
You're just gonna do ODB dirty like that?

3638
04:05:34,520 --> 04:05:35,960
Well, I guess he's already dirty.

3639
04:05:36,080 --> 04:05:36,880
He's an old dirty bastard.

3640
04:05:38,680 --> 04:05:39,960
Yeah, Rosie's great.

3641
04:05:42,440 --> 04:05:43,860
Did we not have Jim this episode?

3642
04:05:43,960 --> 04:05:44,560
We did have Jim.

3643
04:05:46,040 --> 04:05:47,280
We had Jim at the very end.

3644
04:05:51,500 --> 04:05:55,560
I'm imagining someone new joining this stream, reading this chat.

3645
04:05:56,880 --> 04:05:58,460
They're like, wait, did we not have Jim?

3646
04:06:00,880 --> 04:06:01,840
What does that even mean?

3647
04:06:06,700 --> 04:06:07,500
Oh, man.

3648
04:06:09,380 --> 04:06:10,580
Will you ever name Pig 2?

3649
04:06:11,560 --> 04:06:13,740
Uh... I think you just named him.

3650
04:06:14,660 --> 04:06:15,900
That is now his name.

3651
04:06:16,060 --> 04:06:16,920
Thank you, TabSmack.

3652
04:06:18,000 --> 04:06:19,180
It'll be Jim 2.

3653
04:06:19,380 --> 04:06:20,140
I mean, Pig 2!

3654
04:06:20,260 --> 04:06:20,520
Fuck!

3655
04:06:20,640 --> 04:06:21,580
I have Jim on my mind.

3656
04:06:23,880 --> 04:06:24,720
What is a Jim?

3657
04:06:25,060 --> 04:06:26,460
Who are these maniacs?

3658
04:06:26,860 --> 04:06:28,160
I couldn't tell you.

3659
04:06:29,500 --> 04:06:32,080
In fact, I don't think anyone really knows who Jim is.

3660
04:06:33,020 --> 04:06:34,380
We know who Jim is not.

3661
04:06:35,050 --> 04:06:38,070
It is not the main character of a certain game.

3662
04:06:38,190 --> 04:06:39,190
That is not Minecraft.

3663
04:06:50,000 --> 04:06:52,480
The Stanley Parable Dev released a new game yesterday.

3664
04:06:52,660 --> 04:06:52,980
Really?

3665
04:06:54,640 --> 04:06:55,340
No way.

3666
04:06:56,100 --> 04:06:56,960
Is it a good one?

3667
04:06:58,160 --> 04:06:58,840
What is it?

3668
04:07:01,460 --> 04:07:01,880
Wanderstop.

3669
04:07:04,120 --> 04:07:05,800
Oh wait, people told me about this already.

3670
04:07:08,940 --> 04:07:09,780
Oh yeah, yeah.

3671
04:07:10,060 --> 04:07:11,260
People told me about this last time.

3672
04:07:16,590 --> 04:07:16,970
Cool.

3673
04:07:16,970 --> 04:07:19,350
May have to check it out, put it on my backlog.

3674
04:07:23,910 --> 04:07:25,070
The Stanley Fable.

3675
04:07:28,650 --> 04:07:30,130
C418 did the music too, huh?

3676
04:07:31,010 --> 04:07:31,370
Damn.

3677
04:07:34,650 --> 04:07:36,190
It's like a mix of all the good stuff.

3678
04:07:36,370 --> 04:07:37,670
One great cocktail, huh?

3679
04:07:38,850 --> 04:07:39,970
Let's see if it pays off.

3680
04:07:46,420 --> 04:07:49,040
I've played a little bit of Stardew Valley, Nathaniel.

3681
04:07:50,400 --> 04:07:51,660
With my ex, actually.

3682
04:07:51,760 --> 04:07:54,840
One of my... Yeah.

3683
04:07:55,260 --> 04:07:56,240
We played a little bit.

3684
04:07:56,520 --> 04:07:57,260
It was fun.

3685
04:07:58,560 --> 04:07:59,940
Very, very chillaxing.

3686
04:08:02,060 --> 04:08:04,680
Valheim, I want to wait until it's fully released until I play it.

3687
04:08:04,840 --> 04:08:06,680
It's still in early access, as far as I'm aware.

3688
04:08:12,620 --> 04:08:14,320
So Oliver, how do you feel about this stream?

3689
04:08:14,440 --> 04:08:15,820
I'm super happy about this stream.

3690
04:08:17,280 --> 04:08:19,220
I love the fact that I got my items back.

3691
04:08:19,360 --> 04:08:20,600
I'm so ecstatic about it.

3692
04:08:20,920 --> 04:08:21,600
So pumped.

3693
04:08:24,820 --> 04:08:28,120
In fact, I'm just excited for the stuff I want to do next time already.

3694
04:08:28,460 --> 04:08:29,400
I already have an idea.

3695
04:08:30,800 --> 04:08:31,880
Not gonna say, though.

3696
04:08:33,000 --> 04:08:34,120
It'll be a surprise.

3697
04:08:35,640 --> 04:08:36,520
Ralturo, you're late!

3698
04:08:36,660 --> 04:08:36,900
No!

3699
04:08:38,080 --> 04:08:39,200
We're ending right now.

3700
04:08:39,880 --> 04:08:42,540
In fact, I'm saying goodbye in, like, 14 seconds from now.

3701
04:08:46,100 --> 04:08:48,180
I don't know what happened this stream, but I'm happy for you.

3702
04:08:48,280 --> 04:08:48,660
Oh, man.

3703
04:08:49,460 --> 04:08:51,160
All the things happened this stream.

3704
04:08:54,040 --> 04:08:56,280
The Vought Gang is gonna have a field day with this one.

3705
04:08:57,460 --> 04:08:58,820
Alright guys, that's it for me.

3706
04:08:59,640 --> 04:09:00,820
Thank you so much for watching.

3707
04:09:02,100 --> 04:09:05,460
I will now go away and leave you.

3708
04:09:07,720 --> 04:09:09,060
And I'll see you in the next one.

3709
04:09:09,980 --> 04:09:10,660
Very soon.

3710
04:09:11,760 --> 04:09:13,060
Okay, love you all.

3711
04:09:13,920 --> 04:09:14,480
Good night.

